diff -ruN phase25_base/PLANNING_PORTAL_RESILIENCE.md phase25_work/PLANNING_PORTAL_RESILIENCE.md
--- phase25_base/PLANNING_PORTAL_RESILIENCE.md	2026-08-05 23:25:42.000000000 +0000
+++ phase25_work/PLANNING_PORTAL_RESILIENCE.md	2026-08-06 06:36:04.089226843 +0000
@@ -7,3 +7,10 @@
 - A bounded Alton Towers metadata snapshot from the official major-applications register keeps known references visible when the live portal is unavailable. Snapshot records never claim documents or geometry.
 - `planning-coverage-policy=fail` stops world packaging after QA artifacts are written when minimum live applications or downloaded documents are not met.
 - Private builds should use `planning-vector-fusion-mode=private`; unknown-licence council-derived vectors remain explicitly non-redistributable and raw documents stay cache-only.
+
+## Phase 25 enforcement and TLS compatibility
+
+- The pipeline enforces the coverage policy resolved inside the planning catalogue, even when the CLI did not explicitly repeat `--planning-coverage-policy fail`.
+- The two official Staffordshire Moorlands hosts use a three-stage curl ladder after Node fetch fails: normal verified TLS, verified TLS with legacy cipher compatibility, then a host-allowlisted `--insecure` request.
+- Certificate verification bypass is never available to arbitrary hosts. It is recorded as `bypassed-for-allowlisted-official-host`, remains HTTPS-only, and retrieved HTML must pass planning-content validation before it is parsed.
+- PDF and image downloads remain MIME-sniffed, hash-recorded, cache-only, and subject to the existing private-use and planning-authority gates.
